  "voting_summary": "Wisconsin offers two weeks of in-person absentee voting and no-excuse mail, but like Pennsylvania it cannot process any absentee ballots before 7 a.m. on election day; results publish as combined totals. Polls close at 9 p.m. Eastern; election day precincts report through the night, and central-count cities release absentee results late, Milwaukee's absentee dump traditionally lands between 3 and 5 a.m., delivering a final Democratic surge. Ballots must arrive by election day, so the count is complete by the following morning despite the late-night drama.",
